## Enhancing Multicomponent Metal-Organic Frameworks for Low Pressure Liquid Organic Hydrogen Carrier Separations
## Introduction
Cycloalkanes, such as cyclohexane and methylcyclohexane, are essential components of the chemical and petrochemical industries.1 Of significant importance is their application as Liquid Organic Hydrogen Carriers (LOHCs) to safely store and transport hydrogen.2-4 These LOHCs are hydrogenated for hydrogen storage, and then dehydrogenated upon demand to release hydrogen.3, 4 The cyclohexane-benzene-hydrogen and the methylcyclohexane-toluene-hydrogen cycles are the most conventional examples, although the former is not as industrially relevant due to the carcinogenic properties of benzene.2, 4 As the oxidation process to release hydrogen proceeds, the concentration of methylcyclohexane becomes limited, and hence
